  "mechanicsLocks": {
    "launcherCenterSlotGeometry": "Launcher center-slot geometry lock: the launcher has exactly two short, close-set engagement prongs symmetric about its central axis. Both prongs enter the paired launcher slots immediately beside the Beyblade's central Bit Chip/center gap, one on each side of the axis. They never attach to the outer Attack Ring, Weight Disk, perimeter, or tip. Before release the top is level, flush, and firmly retained on both prongs; at release both prongs disengage together and the top becomes fully unsupported, descending tip-first under gravity.",
    "releaseGravity": "After both prongs disengage, a clear air gap remains; no string or tether; the top descends tip-first under gravity.",
    "stadiumMotion": "A spinning top translates continuously across the bowl and cannot stick to a slope.",
    "stoppedTop": "A free non-spinning top falls and lies on its side; it cannot balance upright on its tip."
  },
